# This file is intended for use with Admin API 3 (V3) running against a
# local ODS/API instance. Update the vendorId/claimSetName/dataStoreIds
# values below to match IDs that exist in your environment - use the GET
# requests to look them up.
#
# ADMINAPI-1484: PUT /v3/applications/{id} no longer accepts "enabled" or
# "dataStoreIds" - both are per-ApiClient concerns now, and the request body
# rejects them with a 400 rather than silently ignoring them (the request
# schema declares additionalProperties:false, and this endpoint now actually
# enforces it). Use PUT /v3/apiClients/{id} to change an individual
# credential's approval state or data-store assignment.
# PUT /v3/applications/{id}/reset-credential now returns 409 Conflict once an
# Application has more than one ApiClient (or none at all); use
# PUT /v3/apiClients/{id}/reset-credential for a specific credential instead.

@adminapi_url=https://localhost/adminapi
@adminapi_client=adminapi_client
@adminapi_secret=adminapi_SECRET_2025_rftyguhijkotgyhuijok

### Register a new client
POST {{adminapi_url}}/connect/register
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

ClientId={{adminapi_client}}&ClientSecret={{adminapi_secret}}&DisplayName=Admin+API+{{adminapi_client}}

### Get a token
# @name tokenRequest
POST {{adminapi_url}}/connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded
Authorization: basic {{adminapi_client}}:{{adminapi_secret}}

grant_type=client_credentials&scope=edfi_admin_api/full_access

###
@token={{tokenRequest.response.body.access_token}}


### Get vendors (grab a vendorId to use below)
GET {{adminapi_url}}/v3/vendors
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: bearer {{token}}

### Create vendor without namespace
POST {{adminapi_url}}/v3/vendors
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: bearer {{token}}
Tenant: tenant2

{
  "company": "vendor1",
  "contactName": "David Jiménez",
  "contactEmailAddress": "david.jimenez@example.com"
}

### Get data stores (grab a dataStoreId to use below)
GET {{adminapi_url}}/v3/dataStores
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: bearer {{token}}

### Get claim sets (grab a claimSetName to use below)
GET {{adminapi_url}}/v3/claimSets
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: bearer {{token}}

### Make a copy of a claimset
# @name copyClaimSet
POST {{adminapi_url}}/v3/claimSets/copy
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: bearer {{token}}

{
  "originalId": 2,
  "name": "EdFiSandboxCopy"
}

### Create an Application - send twice to test duplicate (VendorId, ApplicationName) rejection (ADMINAPI-1483: second call should return 400, "already exists for this vendor")
# @name createApplication
POST {{adminapi_url}}/v3/applications
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: bearer {{token}}

{
  "applicationName": "Application1",
  "vendorId": 1,
  "claimSetName": "EdFiSandboxCopy",
  "educationOrganizationIds": [1],
  "dataStoreIds": [
    1
  ]
}

### Get Applications
GET {{adminapi_url}}/v3/applications
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: bearer {{token}}

### Get application
GET {{createApplication.response.headers.Location}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: bearer {{token}}

### Update Application
PUT {{createApplication.response.headers.Location}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: bearer {{token}}

{
  "id": {{createApplication.response.body.id}},
  "applicationName": "Application1 - updated",
  "vendorId": 1,
  "claimSetName": "EdFiSandboxCopy",
  "educationOrganizationIds": [1]
}


### Get application - confirm enabled/dataStoreIds were not changed by the request above
GET {{createApplication.response.headers.Location}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: bearer {{token}}

### Update Application with enabled/dataStoreIds - ADMINAPI-1484: these fields are not part of
### this contract (additionalProperties:false), so this returns 400 instead of applying or
### ignoring them.
PUT {{createApplication.response.headers.Location}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: bearer {{token}}

{
  "id": {{createApplication.response.body.id}},
  "applicationName": "Application1 - updated",
  "vendorId": 1,
  "claimSetName": "EdFiSandboxCopy",
  "educationOrganizationIds": [1],
  "enabled": false,
  "dataStoreIds": [1]
}

### Get ApiClients
GET {{adminapi_url}}/v3/apiClients
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: bearer {{token}}

### Add a second ApiClient to the Application, so the Application has more than one credential -
### this is what makes the "Reset application secret" request below return 409 Conflict.
# @name addApiClient
POST {{adminapi_url}}/v3/apiClients
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: bearer {{token}}

{
  "name": "Second Credential",
  "isApproved": true,
  "applicationId": {{createApplication.response.body.id}},
  "dataStoreIds": [
    1
  ]
}

### Reset application secret - ADMINAPI-1484: now returns 409 Conflict because the Application
### has more than one ApiClient. Use PUT /v3/apiClients/{id}/reset-credential (below) instead.
PUT {{createApplication.response.headers.Location}}/reset-credential
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: bearer {{token}}

### Reset the second ApiClient's secret directly - this is the per-credential path the 409 above
### points to, and it still works exactly as before regardless of how many credentials exist.
PUT {{addApiClient.response.headers.Location}}/reset-credential
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: bearer {{token}}

### Delete application
DELETE {{createApplication.response.headers.Location}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: bearer {{token}}
